{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_607406902#0_1293169683","relevance":3,"reason":"This Mayo Clinic article is dedicated to stress, depression, and the holidays and directly explains why holidays may not feel festive: stress and depression can ruin holidays, and holiday demands such as cooking, shopping, baking, cleaning, entertaining, changed plans, health worries, and COVID-related disruption can add stress, sadness, or anxiety.","learned":"Holiday festivity can be undermined by overwhelming practical demands, health worries, disrupted plans, stress, sadness, anxiety, and depression."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3287","reason":"This holiday-blues/stress query is producing highly authoritative, directly relevant evidence, so continuing is likely to find more grade-3 results."}}
