{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ holidays christmas) (+ stress depression) (+ expectations perfectionism pressure))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_788952568#0_1665434899","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3290","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_788952568#0_1665434899\" , \"end_char\": 1435.000000 , \"headings\": \"How to reduce Christmas stress How to reduce <cover>Christmas stress 1. Limit spending 2. Manage expectations</cover>Be realistic Help children to be realistic Take some time out 3. Avoid overindulging 4. Go for a walk 5. Have some fun \" , \"segment\": \"5 life hacks for a stress-free Christmas How to reduce Christmas stress Written by Hannah Nichols on December 7, 2017 — Fact checked by Jasmin Collier “It’s the most wonderful time of the year,” but also a time when stress levels soar. We have put together some top tips to stop stress in its tracks and make the season of goodwill more enjoyable. Share on Pinterest While Christmas is known as “the season to be jolly,” it can be a significant source of stress, pressure, and conflict for many of us. Some people can feel overwhelmed by the excess, expectations, and exchange and become depressed during the holidays. A lack of time and money, credit card debt, and the pressure of gift "}}
