{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1563327572#8_3187306336","relevance":3,"reason":"This passage is from a dedicated holiday depression/SAD coping article and directly explains why holidays may not feel festive: financial stress, isolation, loneliness, unrealistic expectations, over-commercialization, pressure to feel constant cheer, hectic schedules, and year-end regret or perceived failure can create holiday stress and sadness.","learned":"Holidays can feel less festive because commercialized expectations of nonstop cheer create pressure, while financial strain, loneliness, unrealistic hopes, and year-end reflection add sadness and stress."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3290","reason":"The current query is producing strong evidence about holiday stress, expectations, and depression; continue to collect additional grade-3 results if available."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3290"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_788952568#1_1665436839","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3290","rank":3,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_788952568#1_1665436839\" , \"end_char\": 2081.000000 , \"headings\": \"How to reduce Christmas stress How to reduce <cover>Christmas stress 1. Limit spending 2. Manage expectations</cover>Be realistic Help children to be realistic Take some time out 3. Avoid overindulging 4. Go for a walk 5. Have some fun \" , \"segment\": \"Most of us are aware of the adverse effects that stress can have on our body. It can impact our thoughts, feelings, and behaviors, and it can lead to high blood pressure, heart disease, diabetes, and obesity if left unchecked. In fact, research has shown that there is an increase in the occurrence of heart attacks and heart-related deaths during the festive season, which may be due to stress, heavy alcohol consumption, a fatty diet, or all three. Therefore, it is of utmost importance that holiday stress is dealt with — pronto. With all the cooking, decorating, visiting, and gift giving, the holidays can seem more like trying to meet a high-pressure deadline than a vacation. So, try these Christmas stress-busting "}}
{"request":{"judgments":"22/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_788952568#1_1665436839","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another passage from the dedicated Medical News Today article on reducing Christmas stress. It directly supports why holidays may not feel festive by explaining that cooking, decorating, visiting, and gift-giving can make holidays feel like a high-pressure deadline rather than a vacation, with stress compounded by heavy alcohol consumption and rich food.","learned":"Holiday tasks and obligations can turn the festive season into a stressful deadline, reducing enjoyment and contributing to health and emotional strain."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3290","reason":"The query on holiday stress, expectations, and pressure is yielding directly relevant evidence; continue to find more grade-3 passages or sources."}}
