{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1234831183#1_2482174999","relevance":3,"reason":"This article is dedicated to holiday-season stress and coping, and the passage directly explains why holidays may not feel festive: cooking, cleaning, gift shopping, unrealistic expectations, and stress can keep people from appreciating family time and enjoying the season.","learned":"Holiday chores, gift shopping, and lofty expectations can overwhelm people and make the season feel stressful instead of festive."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3291","reason":"The holiday-season stress/loneliness query is producing direct evidence about causes of unfestive holidays; continue for more grade-3 results."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3291"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_12_1234831183#0_2482172696","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3291","rank":3,"snippet":"time of year when the PTO is plentiful, the snacks and sweets never stop coming, and family and friends are always by your side. However, those final weeks that mark the end of the year are also marked by one not-so-pleasant thing: holiday stress. All that cooking, cleaning, and gift shopping can get to even the most resilient of us, which is why we've asked psychologists for their top tips on dealing with these woes. What results is an incredibly helpful guide for getting through year's end with your mental health intact. And for more ways to combat stress, check out these 15 Magical Phrases and Words That Help Relieve <cover>Stress. 1 Manage your expectations. Shutterstock While the holiday season </cover>can be an incredibly joyful experience for most, many of you likely spend more time reeling from the stress of cooking, cleaning, and purchasing gifts to fully appreciate the time spent with family.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"17 Top Tips from Psychologists for Dealing with Holiday Stress | Best Life\" , \"url\": \"https://bestlifeonline.com/holiday-stress/\" }"}}
