{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_1528043899#0_3275666494","relevance":3,"reason":"This NAMI article is dedicated to managing mental health during the holidays and directly explains why holidays may not feel festive: the season can worsen stress, anxiety, and depression due to financial burdens from travel/gifts/hosting, packed calendars, difficulty balancing responsibilities and self-care, high expectations for perfect gifts/events, and loneliness away from loved ones.","learned":"Holiday anxiety and depression can stem from financial burden, overpacked schedules, neglected self-care, perfectionistic expectations, and loneliness."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3291","reason":"The current query is retrieving strong, dedicated holiday-season stress and loneliness evidence; continue to find additional grade-3 results."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3291"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1169685536#13_1682249295","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3291","rank":5,"snippet":"Tips 8 Daily Relapse Prevention Tips Table of contents 8 Addiction Relapse Prevention Tips Holiday Relapse Prevention Tips 1. Treat it like any other day. 2. Manage expectations. 3. Stay in close contact with your sponsor. 4. Plan carefully. 5. Turn down invitations if necessary. 6. Practice healthy stress management. 7. Ask for help when you need it. Why are Relapse Prevention Tips and Strategies Important? Contact us today. We can help. 512.363.5914 Discover Eudaimonia Our Locations Gender-Specific Homes \" , \"segment\": \"2. Manage expectations. Having unrealistic <cover>expectations about the holiday season can cause a great deal of stress, </cover>which can increase your risk of relapsing. Instead of expecting everything to be perfect, know that the holiday season will likely have some hiccups. Things may not go exactly as you planned, you may be hit with some severe cravings, and you may not even feel happy or joyful at all. Although it would be nice, a picture-perfect holiday is unlikely to happen, but realistic expectations make it easier to roll with the punches. 3. Stay in close contact with your sponsor. The holidays can be hard, especially if you’re newly sober, "}}
