{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_57_551394404#6_748757573","relevance":0,"reason":"This result is about post-travel or post-vacation depression after returning from a trip, not seasonal holidays feeling unfestive or less magical.","learned":"Queries using 'post holiday depression' can drift to vacation/travel depression rather than holiday-season blues."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ christmas (+ childhood child kids) (+ nostalgia nostalgic memories) (+ magic magical))","reason":"Search for evidence that holidays feel less festive because adults compare them to childhood nostalgia and the lost magic of being a child, a likely direct explanation not yet well covered."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ christmas (+ childhood child kids) (+ nostalgia nostalgic memories) (+ magic magical))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_392326660#13_355938468","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3298","rank":1,"snippet":"and universities High schools Media/press Radio Emergency alert stations Notable people References External links \" , \"segment\": \"From her childhood memories, Sherry Lynn Mason recalls the Land O' Toys: \\\"I loved that store. Every time [my father] took me there, we were waiting for his outboard motor to be fixed across the street. It was a magical place to me!\\\" Amy Berry Baker recalls, \\\"It wasn't Christmas until we went to Howard Griffin ... magical for kids,\\\" according to an article in The Monroe News-Star. Mrs. Griffin died December 15, 1985, and the store closed permanently a few days after <cover>Christmas of that year. In March 2011, the remaining abandoned building burned. All that remains are the memories of the former customers, now all adults. Cheri Chadduck recalled, \"Memories are completely magical, and I am so grateful for my childhood </cover>recollections of time there.\" Art Deco style Federal Building & U.S. Courthouse in Monroe 2020 tornado See also:\" , \"start_char\": 7155.000000 , \"title\": \"Monroe, Louisiana - Wikipedia\" , \"url\": \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monroe,_Louisiana\" }"}}
